[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186097262 :question/answer-fields 17592186095496] {:db/id 17592186096632 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0eabe319-fbfe-5f66-832c-db699322266a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096631 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fea7dc0c-332b-5e65-b34c-aa74602e656a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186393250 :question/problem "What is ${\\int }_{e}^{3e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{e}^{3e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ the lower bound is $a=e,$ and the upper bound is $b=3e.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3e-e}{n}=\\frac{2e}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e}^{3e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(e+i\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(e+\\frac{2ie}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+\\frac{2ie}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186393254 :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+\\frac{2ie}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186393252 :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+\\frac{4ie}{n})\\cdot \\frac{4e}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186393256 :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+\\frac{ie}{n})\\cdot \\frac{e}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fea7dc0c-332b-5e65-b34c-aa74602e656a" :question/id #uuid "fea7dc0c-332b-5e65-b34c-aa74602e656a" :question/math-academy-id "q-113885" :question/problem "What is ${\\int }_{2}^{4}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{4}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=(x+1)^{2},$ the lower bound is $a=2,$ and the upper bound is $b=4.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-2}{n}=\\frac{2}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(2+i\\cdot \\frac{2}{n})\\,\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(2+\\frac{2i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(2+\\frac{2i}{n}+1)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(3+\\frac{2i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2bc5e161-63d6-5b2f-8b4b-8f2692b551e3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2bc5e161-63d6-5b2f-8b4b-8f2692b551e3" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bc5e161-63d6-5b2f-8b4b-8f2692b551e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-34501985-19ea-50dc-8d60-3b788c0405c5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-51e949c9-0d0e-5fdb-bb95-ab16798be0f2" "answer-dfa0ac59-d407-5702-ab18-aa0299efd7dc" "answer-6591ea6e-2346-5c79-acf4-89b87782b7b7" "answer-34501985-19ea-50dc-8d60-3b788c0405c5" "answer-28f1f4b7-57c0-56e1-a117-8415a85c841e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51e949c9-0d0e-5fdb-bb95-ab16798be0f2" :answer/id #uuid "51e949c9-0d0e-5fdb-bb95-ab16798be0f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(1+\\frac{2i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfa0ac59-d407-5702-ab18-aa0299efd7dc" :answer/id #uuid "dfa0ac59-d407-5702-ab18-aa0299efd7dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(1+\\frac{4i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6591ea6e-2346-5c79-acf4-89b87782b7b7" :answer/id #uuid "6591ea6e-2346-5c79-acf4-89b87782b7b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(1+\\frac{i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34501985-19ea-50dc-8d60-3b788c0405c5" :answer/id #uuid "34501985-19ea-50dc-8d60-3b788c0405c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(3+\\frac{2i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28f1f4b7-57c0-56e1-a117-8415a85c841e" :answer/id #uuid "28f1f4b7-57c0-56e1-a117-8415a85c841e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(3+\\frac{2i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0eabe319-fbfe-5f66-832c-db699322266a" :question/id #uuid "0eabe319-fbfe-5f66-832c-db699322266a" :question/math-academy-id "q-114899" :question/problem "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that ${\\int }_{2}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[4{(2+\\frac{k}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}].$" :question/worked-solution "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=2.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{1}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{n}=\\frac{b-2}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nConsequently,  ${x}_{k}=2+\\frac{k}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})=4{x}_{k}^{3}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{3}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[4{(2+\\frac{k}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(x)=4{x}^{3}$ and $b=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0a33f6fd-b93c-5b4f-b219-979a3489cf29"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0a33f6fd-b93c-5b4f-b219-979a3489cf29" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a33f6fd-b93c-5b4f-b219-979a3489cf29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a2a12a2b-40b0-5e22-9231-966dc3b78cb8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b72f4429-d885-5f60-880a-67e28d6f6c64" "answer-a2a12a2b-40b0-5e22-9231-966dc3b78cb8" "answer-ace7f773-c717-5546-8619-944725dddd02" "answer-726d3224-ba57-579d-ae29-183da135a7ac" "answer-67ea339c-2b2b-5d4d-87b1-7c6bc85069c4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b72f4429-d885-5f60-880a-67e28d6f6c64" :answer/id #uuid "b72f4429-d885-5f60-880a-67e28d6f6c64" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)=4x$ and $b=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2a12a2b-40b0-5e22-9231-966dc3b78cb8" :answer/id #uuid "a2a12a2b-40b0-5e22-9231-966dc3b78cb8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)=4{x}^{3}$ and $b=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ace7f773-c717-5546-8619-944725dddd02" :answer/id #uuid "ace7f773-c717-5546-8619-944725dddd02" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)=4{x}^{3}$ and $b=5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-726d3224-ba