{4}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?"] ["question-fea7dc0c-332b-5e65-b34c-aa74602e656a" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{4}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=(x+1)^{2},$ the lower bound is $a=2,$ and the upper bound is $b=4.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-2}{n}=\\frac{2}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(2+i\\cdot \\frac{2}{n})\\,\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(2+\\frac{2i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(2+\\frac{2i}{n}+1)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(3+\\frac{2i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-fea7dc0c-332b-5e65-b34c-aa74602e656a" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-2bc5e161-63d6-5b2f-8b4b-8f2692b551e3" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bc5e161-63d6-5b2f-8b4b-8f2692b551e3"] ["answer-51e949c9-0d0e-5fdb-bb95-ab16798be0f2" :answer/id #uuid "51e949c9-0d0e-5fdb-bb95-ab16798be0f2"] ["answer-51e949c9-0d0e-5fdb-bb95-ab16798be0f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-51e949c9-0d0e-5fdb-bb95-ab16798be0f2" :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(1+\\frac{2i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]"] ["answer-dfa0ac59-d407-5702-ab18-aa0299efd7dc" :answer/id #uuid "dfa0ac59-d407-5702-ab18-aa0299efd7dc"] ["answer-dfa0ac59-d407-5702-ab18-aa0299efd7dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-dfa0ac59-d407-5702-ab18-aa0299efd7dc" :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\