32b-5e65-b34c-aa74602e656a" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-2bc5e161-63d6-5b2f-8b4b-8f2692b551e3"] [17592186096631 :knowledge-point/questions "question-fea7dc0c-332b-5e65-b34c-aa74602e656a"] ["question-0eabe319-fbfe-5f66-832c-db699322266a" :question/id #uuid "0eabe319-fbfe-5f66-832c-db699322266a"] ["question-0eabe319-fbfe-5f66-832c-db699322266a" :question/math-academy-id "q-114899"] ["question-0eabe319-fbfe-5f66-832c-db699322266a" :question/problem "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that ${\\int }_{2}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[4{(2+\\frac{k}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}].$"] ["question-0eabe319-fbfe-5f66-832c-db699322266a" :question/worked-solution "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=2.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{1}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{n}=\\frac{b-2}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nConsequently,  ${x}_{k}=2+\\frac{k}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})=4{x}_{k}^{3}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{3}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[4{(2+\\frac{k}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(x)=4{x}^{3}$ and $b=3.$"] ["question-0eabe319-fbfe-5f66-832c-db699322266a" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-0a33f6fd-b93c-5b4f-b219-979a3489cf29" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a33f6fd-b93c-5b4f-b219-979a3489cf29"] ["answer-b72f4429-d885-5f60-880a-67e28d6f6c64" :answer/id #uuid "b72f4429-d885-5f60-880a-67e28d6f6c64"] ["answer-b72f4429-d885-5f60-880a-67e28d6f6c64" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-b72f4429-d885-5f60-880a-67e28d6f6c64" :answer/value "$f(x)=4x$ and $b=3$"] ["answer-a2a12a2b-40b0-5e22-9231-966dc3b78cb8" :answer/id 